invariant: INV-14
file: webpki.c
catches: webpki_chain_test
reason: read_issuer skips the clock check on an intermediate, so a chain
  under an expired or not-yet-valid CA certificate verifies whenever
  its leaf is valid (docs/webpki.md, "The chain walk", step 6d). The
  issuer_expired and issuer_not_yet_valid rows, whose leaf is valid at
  the row's clock and whose intermediate is not, object.

--- old
    if (!validity_covers(issuer, now)) {
        *alert = ALERT_CERTIFICATE_EXPIRED;
        return CH_EAUTH;
    }
    if (!names_equal(issuer->subject, issuer->subject_len, cert->issuer, cert->issuer_len)) {
--- new
